"dial theming" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Dial
		<header>A dial lets people pick a number by turning it, with its value in the middle and its label under it.</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-dial-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` included), or on the
			dial's box through `::part(dial)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. Style the pieces with `::part()`: `track`, `track-fill`, `handle`,
			`disc`, `ticks`, `value` and `label`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-dial {
			  --ui-dial-size: 8em;
			  --ui-dial-track-width: 6;
			}
			ui-dial::part(value) {
			  font-weight: 600;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`--ui-dial-size` is the dial's width; `--ui-dial-track-width` the ring's, in its 100-wide drawing's units; `color`
				replaces `--ui-dial-fill-color`; a size scales the whole dial. The value's type follows the dial's width. Never
				set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-dial" playground>
				<ui-dial label="Volume" color="blue" value="40" ticks></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes the colours a dial inherits.</>
	</>
